[Music]  or bolt-action rifles to shotguns  there's something in battlefield one to  fit all play styles but what about those  level 10 weapons for each class on  average it will take you a few weeks  grinding in a single class to unlock  just one of these rare weapons so how do  you know if any of them are worth  grinding for don't worry we're here to  help you decide which level 10 weapon is  right for you  the martini-henry with max out damage  and accuracy at first glance this rifle  appears to be a one-hit killing machine  this gun hits for high damage on the  body but my problem with it is the long  reload animation I know this may sound  funny but picture this when using a  rater of bolt-action rifle the bolt  cycle animation between shots takes less  than a second the Henry is breech  loading 1 slow round at a time that few  seconds leaves you wide open and close  to medium range if you don't kill your  target with the first shot also for  those of you who love using scoped  rifles sorry this rifle is an iron sight  only it's a cool gun and packs the power  but I really found myself returning to  some of my old bolt-action rifles such  as the smle MK 3 infantry for better  reliability but has a nice side bonus  once you reach a level 10 as the Scout  you unlock the baby pistol isn't it cute  the problem is you really can't kill  with it  next up is the sub slaughter 1906  factory rifle for the medic class if you  ever used an m1 grand and pass  battlefield games you'll feel right at  home with this gun with good damage and  high accuracy this weapon became my  favorite accessory to a med pack the  downside to this weapon just like the m1  grand is that it only has 5 rounds per  clip three shots to the chest will kill  your foe and the remaining rounds can be  used to kill an enemy at half health  this rifle isn't the best in outnumbered  moments like the other medic rifles such  as the m-19 o 7 SL sweeper by the  autoloading 8.25 extended but this gun  is well worth the grinding if being a  medic is your style the level chugging  gun you most likely will see on the  field is the hell réguel 1915 factory  SMG for the assault class packing a  monstrous rate of fire and control this  SMG is one of the best guns you can grab  for your assault however that doesn't  mean this weapon doesn't have its faults  for starters it packs a 60 round  magazine but you only have 60 rounds  left in reserve so unless you're near a  support handing out ammunition you're  going to be running out of ammo fast  also to note that despite the rate of  fire it packs low damage and decent  accuracy so is this gun really worth it  for the assault class absolutely  if you willing to deal with the  ammunition drawbacks  last but not least is the hold automatic  lightweight LMG for the support class on  paper this thing is a beast with  best-in-class accuracy but as anyone who  plays Battlefield knows you don't judge  a gun by its stats the hold also sports  hefty spread or even with the bipod  deployed an earlier unlock the bar is  better at putting up high damage rounds  on a target at close range and the Lewis  gun with high ammo capacity relatively  fast reloads performs better at range  the low ammo count for this weapon also  hurts the LMG class where weapons become  more accurate the longer they are fired  if you love handing out boxes of ammo by  all means play the support but if you're  grinding to level 10 this gun just  doesn't live up to the stats and there  you have it folks for rare level 10 guns  to sink your teeth into at the end of  the day go after the gun that best fits  your play style and I'll see you on the  battlefield for more on your favorite  games keep it here on GameSpot

